  <media:group>
   <media:title>Range Rover Sport Electric | Inside the Peak to Peak Challenge</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/mYLx9sjFLxU?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i2.ytimg.com/vi/mYLx9sjFLxU/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>Hear the story from the front seat.

After almost 30 years behind the wheel for Range Rover, Andy Maskell has seen a lot.

Closely involved in the development of Range Rover Sport Electric, Andy knows how the vehicle responds and what the technology can do.

The Peak to Peak Challenge is where that knowledge meets the real world. Across the Carrara quarries in Italy, Range Rover Sport Electric navigates slippery marble dust, steep climbs and tight, twisting roads, putting the vehicles traction, control and electric capability to the test.

No artificial test environment, no computer-generated terrain, and no modified conditions. Just a production vehicle, a highly experienced development driver, and one of the world's most demanding landscapes.

Driving from peak to peak through active marble quarries means navigating sheer drops, sharp rock surfaces, and a fine layer of marble powder that reduces grip and constantly changes beneath the tyres. In these conditions, Intelligent Torque Management constantly adjusts torque delivery within milliseconds, helping maintain traction and control.

New Range Rover Sport Electric combines exceptional composure with responsive performance, helping create a confident and connected driving experience whether climbing loose quarry tracks, descending steep gradients or threading through twisting mountain roads. A bespoke chassis tune, supported by Dynamic Air Suspension and Adaptive Dynamics, continuously prepares the vehicle for the terrain ahead, helping deliver the dynamic agility, body control and driver confidence that define Range Rover Sport Electric.

This latest challenge continues a long tradition of landmark Range Rover Sport feats. From a record-breaking ascent of Pikes Peak, to conquering Heaven's Gate in China and scaling an Icelandic spillway, Range Rover Sport has consistently demonstrated its ability in environments that push both driver and vehicle to their limits. This time, it’s among the 3,000ft peaks of the Carrara quarries.

Behind the wheel, Andy experienced how smoothly and precisely the vehicle manages traction on challenging surfaces. The result is a vehicle that feels predictable, accurate and confidence-inspiring, even when the terrain becomes increasingly demanding. The responsiveness of the dual electric motors and Intelligent Torque Management help deliver precise, predictable responses, creating a vehicle that feels accurate, confidence-inspiring and composed even as the terrain becomes increasingly demanding.

In Andy's words, there wasn't a single challenge on the route that Range Rover Sport Electric couldn't handle.

Watch the full Peak to Peak Challenge and discover how Range Rover Sport Electric continues the legacy of performance, capability, and all-terrain confidence: https://youtu.be/JzHlw4lxEN0

#RangeRoverSportElectric


